  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "The first section of the Museum collection is largely composed of paintings
    and prints that were removed in 1833 from the abandoned monasteries, charitable
    homes and convents of Porto. The enactment of the decree for the dissolution
    of religious orders, in 1834, allowed the Museum to incorporate the artistic
    assets of the monasteries of S\xE3o Martinho de Tib\xE3es and Santa Cruz de Coimbra.\r\n\r\nThis
    first public art museum in Portugal registed paintings, prints and historical
    objects, such as the series of enamels of the Passion of Christ from the Monastery
    of Santa Cruz de Coimbra.\r\n"
