  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9541d86e2fd84c1d9990edf0852d74ab, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshPro
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Between 1827 and 1833, in Rome, at the culmination of an intense career,
    Domingos Sequeira painted a series of four canvases with a sacred theme: Descent
    from the Cross, Adoration of the Magi, Ascension and Last Judgement.



    Conceptually,
    these four works have in common the depiction of the biblical narrative, always
    faithfully followed, presented as a great spectacle performed by the crowd, with
    the light, sometimes intimate and sometimes overwhelming, as the omnipresent
    protagonist.



    Three of the paintings address the concept of life''s finitude
    and immortality, reflecting the inspired religiosity that accompanied the artist
    near the end of his life.



    These four paintings are considered the peak
    of Sequeira''s work, the ultimate expression of what he considered to be his
    legacy as an artist and a manifesto of his alignment with the avant-garde artistic
    trends of his time.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
